# Event Registration System API

A backend API for managing events and user registrations, built with Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, and JWT authentication.

## 🚀 Features

* User Registration & Login
* JWT Authentication
* Role-Based Access Control (Admin/User)
* Event Creation & Management
* Event Registration System
* Cancel Event Registration
* View User Registrations
* Input Validation with Joi
* Global Error Handling
* MongoDB Database Integration

---

# 🛠️ Tech Stack

* Node.js
* Express.js
* MongoDB
* Mongoose
* JWT Authentication
* Joi Validation
* bcryptjs

---

# 📁 Project Structure

```bash
src/
  controllers/
  middleware/
  models/
  routes/
  validators/
  config/
```

---

# ⚙️ Installation

## 1. Clone Repository

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
```

## 2. Navigate Into Project

```bash
cd event_registration_system
```

## 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

## 4. Create Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the root directory:

```env
PORT=5000
MONGO_URL=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
```

---

# ▶️ Running the Server

```bash
npm run dev
```

OR

```bash
node app.js
```

Server runs on:

```bash
http://localhost:5000
```

---

# 🔐 Authentication

Authentication is handled using JWT tokens.

Include token in request headers:

```http
Authorization: Bearer your_token_here
```

---

# 📌 API Endpoints

## 👤 Auth Routes

### Register User

```http
POST /api/auth/register
```

### Login User

```http
POST /api/auth/login
```

---

## 📅 Event Routes

### Create Event (Admin Only)

```http
POST /api/events
```

### Get All Events

```http
GET /api/events
```

### Get Single Event

```http
GET /api/events/:id
```

---

## 📝 Registration Routes

### Register For Event

```http
POST /api/registrations/:id/register
```

### Cancel Registration

```http
DELETE /api/registrations/:id/cancel
```

### View My Registrations

```http
GET /api/registrations/me
```

---

# 🛡️ Role-Based Access Control

This project supports two user roles:

* user
* admin

Admins can:

* Create events
* Manage platform resources

Users can:

* View events
* Register for events
* Cancel registrations

---

# ✅ Validation & Error Handling

The API uses Joi validation middleware to validate incoming requests and centralized error handling for consistent API responses.

---

# ☁️ Deployment

Recommended deployment platforms:

